  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|A semigroup of renormalisation maps>

    \;

    <math|\<frak-R\><rsub|S><around|(|V|)>=-log
    <around|(|\<mu\><rsup|S>\<ast\>\<mathe\><rsup|-V>|)>>. Since
    <math|\<mu\><rsup|S>\<ast\>\<mu\><rsup|S<rprime|'>>=\<mu\><rsup|S+S<rprime|'>>>,

    <\equation*>
      \<frak-R\><rsub|S>\<circ\>\<frak-R\><rsub|S<rprime|'>>=\<frak-R\><rsub|S+S<rprime|'>>=\<frak-R\><rsub|S<rprime|'>>\<circ\>\<frak-R\><rsub|S>,<space|2em>V<rsub|t>=\<frak-R\><rsub|S<rsub|t>><around|(|V<rsub|T>|)>:
    </equation*>

    an orbit of an <strong|abelian> semigroup indexed by the cone of positive
    covariances, nonlinear on <math|V>, linear on <math|\<mathe\><rsup|-V>>.
    Generators:

    <\equation*>
      \<cal-P\><rsub|B><around|(|V|)>=<tfrac|1|2><math-up|Tr><around|(|B*\<mathD\><rsup|2>*V|)>-<tfrac|1|2><around|\<langle\>|\<mathD\>V,B*\<mathD\>V|\<rangle\>>,<space|2em>\<partial\><rsub|t>*V<rsub|t>=-\<cal-P\><rsub|<wide|Q|\<dot\>><rsub|t>><around|(|V<rsub|t>|)>.
    </equation*>

    <\proposition*>
      <dueto|Flatness><with|font-shape|right|(formal)>
      <math|<around|[|\<cal-P\><rsub|B>,\<cal-P\><rsub|B<rprime|'>>|]>=0>.
      <math|V<rsub|t>> depends on the profile only through
      <math|S<rsub|t>>; <math|V<rsub|0><around|(|0|)>> and
      <math|\<nu\><rsub|T>> only through <math|Q<rsub|T>>.
    </proposition*>

    Different profiles with the same endpoints are different
    <strong|coordinate systems> on the same RG trajectory: they change
    <math|\<Phi\>> and intermediate observables, not the terminal theory.
    <strong|No holonomy.>
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|Perturbation theory and counterterms>

    <\with|font-size|0.9>
      \;

      Gaussian convolution <strong|lowers the Wick ordering>:
      <math|V<rsub|t>=<big|int><around|[|<frac|\<lambda\>|12>:\<phi\><rsup|4>:<rsub|t>+\<gamma\><rsub|T>:\<phi\><rsup|2>:<rsub|t>|]>+O<around|(|\<lambda\><rsup|2>|)>>
      (<math|\<gamma\><rsub|T>=O<around|(|\<lambda\><rsup|2>|)>>, kept for later use;
      <math|:\<phi\><rsup|p>:<rsub|t>=H<rsub|p><around|(|\<phi\>;c<rsub|t>|)>>, <math|c<rsub|t>=Q<rsub|t><around|(|x,x|)>>):
      dual to <math|<big|int>H<rsub|4>*<around|(|X<rsub|t>;c<rsub|t>|)>> being an observable (Lecture<nbsp>3). At second order, <math|S=S<rsub|t>>:

      <\proposition*>
        <with|font-shape|right|(formal)> To second order in
        <math|\<lambda\>>:

        <\equation*>
          V<rsub|t>=<big|int><around*|[|<frac|\<lambda\>|12>:\<phi\><rsup|4>:<rsub|t>+\<gamma\><rsub|T>:\<phi\><rsup|2>:<rsub|t>|]>-<frac|\<lambda\><rsup|2>|288>*<big|sum><rsub|k=1><rsup|4><binom|4|k><rsup|2>k!<big|iint>S*<around|(|x,y|)><rsup|k><space|0.17em>:\<phi\><rsup|4-k>:<rsub|t><around|(|x|)><space|0.17em>:\<phi\><rsup|4-k>:<rsub|t><around|(|y|)>+O<around|(|\<lambda\><rsup|3>|)>.
        </equation*>
      </proposition*>

      <math|T\<to\>\<infty\>> at fixed <math|t>, <math|d=3>,
      <math|G<around|(|z|)>\<sim\><around|(|4*\<pi\><around|\||z|\|>|)><rsup|-1>> (the kernel of <math|A<rsup|-1>>):

      <\itemize>
        <item><math|k=1,2>: finite, nonlocal.

        <item><math|k=3> (<strong|sunset>):
        <math|S<rsup|3>\<sim\><around|\||z|\|><rsup|-3>>; local divergence
        <math|-<frac|\<lambda\><rsup|2>|3><around|(|<big|int>S<rsup|3>|)>*<big|int>:\<phi\><rsup|2>:<rsub|t>>
        (+ finite), cancelled by <math|\<gamma\><rsub|T>=<frac|\<lambda\><rsup|2>|3>*<big|int>Q<rsub|T><rsup|3>=<frac|\<lambda\><rsup|2>|48*\<pi\><rsup|2>>*log
        T+O<around|(|1|)>>.

        <item><math|k=4>: vacuum energy <math|\<sim\>T>; cancels in
        <math|\<nu\><rsub|T>>.
      </itemize>

      Renormalisation <math|=> choosing <math|V<rsub|T>> so that
      <math|V<rsub|t>> at <strong|fixed> resolution converges.
      <math|\<nu\><rsub|t>\<ll\>\<mu\><rsup|Q<rsub|t>>> expected for
      <math|t\<less\>\<infty\>>; the terminal <math|\<Phi\><rsup|4><rsub|3>>
      is singular w.r.t. the GFF.
    </with>
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
