  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|Stochastic localisation: what and why>

    Eldan 2013: write a measure as a mixture of simpler ones, by a
    measure-valued martingale. Here

    <\equation*>
      \<mu\><rsub|t><rsup|\<phi\>><around|(|\<mathd\>y|)>\<propto\>\<mathe\><rsup|<around|\<langle\>|S<rsub|t><rsup|-1>\<phi\>,y|\<rangle\>>-<frac|1|2><around|\<langle\>|y,\<cal-R\><rsub|t>*y|\<rangle\>>>*\<nu\><rsub|T><around|(|\<mathd\>y|)>,<space|2em>\<Phi\><rsub|t>=J<rsub|t>\<Phi\><rsub|T>+\<zeta\><rsub|t>:
    </equation*>

    <math|\<Phi\><rsub|t>> is a noisy <strong|observation> of
    <math|\<Phi\><rsub|T>>, with precision <math|\<cal-R\><rsub|t>> gained,
    and <math|\<mu\><rsub|t>> the <strong|posterior>. Eldan's
    identity-control case: <math|\<cal-R\><rsub|t>=t\<cdot\>1>.

    <\itemize>
      <item><strong|Martingale:> Itô splits variance and entropy into
      revealed and hidden parts.

      <item><strong|Simpler pieces:> <math|\<nu\><rsub|T>> log-concave
      <math|\<Rightarrow\>> <math|\<mu\><rsub|t>> is
      <math|\<cal-R\><rsub|t>>-uniformly log-concave.

      <item><strong|One quantity:> the loss is governed by
      <math|Cov<rsub|t>>, with explicit dynamics. An inequality reduces to:
      <em|the localisation is not too fast>.

      <item><strong|Algorithms:> sampling
      (El<nbsp>Alaoui\UMontanari\USellke), denoising diffusions (Montanari);
      <math|\<omega\><rsub|t>> is minus the score, seen through
      <math|J<rsub|t>>.
    </itemize>
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|Entropy along the localisation>

    <\with|font-size|0.9>
      <math|\<rho\>\<geqslant\>0>, <math|\<bbb-E\><rsub|\<nu\><rsub|T>>*\<rho\>=1>,
      <math|M<rsub|t>=\<bbb-E\><rsub|t>*\<rho\><around|(|\<Phi\><rsub|T>|)>=G<rsub|t><around|(|\<Phi\><rsub|t>|)>>,
      <math|G<rsub|t><around|(|\<phi\>|)>=<big|int>\<rho\>*\<mathd\>\<mu\><rsub|t><rsup|\<phi\>>>.

      <\itemize>
        <item><math|M<rsub|0>=1>, <math|M<rsub|T>=\<rho\><around|(|\<Phi\><rsub|T>|)>>,
        and <math|\<mathd\>M<rsub|t>=<around|\<langle\>|\<mathD\>G<rsub|t><around|(|\<Phi\><rsub|t>|)>,<wide|Q|\<dot\>><rsub|t><rsup|1/2>*\<mathd\>W<rsub|t>|\<rangle\>>>.

        <item>Itô for <math|M*log M>:

        <\equation*>
          Ent<rsub|\<nu\><rsub|T>><around|(|\<rho\>|)>=<frac|1|2>*\<bbb-E\><big|int><rsub|0><rsup|T><frac|\<mathd\><around|\<langle\>|M|\<rangle\>><rsub|t>|M<rsub|t>>=2*\<bbb-E\><big|int><rsub|0><rsup|T><around*|\<\|\|\>|<wide|Q|\<dot\>><rsub|t><rsup|1/2>*\<mathD\><sqrt|G<rsub|t>><around|(|\<Phi\><rsub|t>|)>|\<\|\|\>><rsup|2>*\<mathd\>t.
        </equation*>

        <item>Stopping at <math|t>: <strong|revealed + hidden> entropy,

        <\equation*>
          Ent<rsub|\<nu\><rsub|T>><around|(|\<rho\>|)>=\<bbb-E\><around|[|M<rsub|t>log M<rsub|t>|]>+\<bbb-E\>*Ent<rsub|\<mu\><rsub|t><rsup|\<Phi\><rsub|t>>><around|(|\<rho\>|)>.
        </equation*>

        <item>The increments see the conditional law:
        <math|\<mathD\>G<rsub|t><around|(|\<phi\>|)>=S<rsub|t><rsup|-1>*Cov<rsub|\<mu\><rsub|t><rsup|\<phi\>>><around|(|\<rho\>,y|)>>.

        <item><strong|Entropic stability> (Chen\UEldan; <math|<wide|\<cal-R\>|\<dot\>><rsub|r>=S<rsub|r><rsup|-1><wide|Q|\<dot\>><rsub|r>S<rsub|r><rsup|-1>>): if
        <math|<wide|\<cal-R\>|\<dot\>><rsub|r>*Cov<rsub|\<mu\><rsub|r><rsup|\<phi\>>>*<wide|\<cal-R\>|\<dot\>><rsub|r>\<leqslant\>\<alpha\><rsub|r>*<wide|\<cal-R\>|\<dot\>><rsub|r>>
        for all <math|\<phi\>> and <math|r\<leqslant\>t>, then
        <math|Ent<rsub|\<nu\><rsub|T>><around|(|\<rho\>|)>\<leqslant\>\<mathe\><rsup|<big|int><rsub|0><rsup|t>\<alpha\><rsub|r>*\<mathd\>r>*\<bbb-E\>*Ent<rsub|\<mu\><rsub|t><rsup|\<Phi\><rsub|t>>><around|(|\<rho\>|)>>:
        the low resolutions must not hide too much.
      </itemize>

      <small|<with|color|dark grey|Bauerschmidt\UBodineau\UDagallier, Probab.
      Surveys 2024: their fluctuation measure is our stochastic localisation
      (scale reversed).>>
    </with>
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|Multiscale Bakry\UÉmery>

    <\with|font-size|0.9>
      <\theorem*>
        <dueto|Bauerschmidt\UBodineau><with|font-shape|right|(formal)> If for
        all <math|t,\<phi\>>, with <math|\<kappa\><rsub|t>\<in\>\<bbb-R\>>
        (possibly negative),

        <\equation*>
          <wide|Q|\<dot\>><rsub|t>*\<mathD\><rsup|2>*V<rsub|t><around|(|\<phi\>|)>*<wide|Q|\<dot\>><rsub|t>+<frac|1|2>*<wide|Q|\<ddot\>><rsub|t>\<geqslant\>\<kappa\><rsub|t>*<wide|Q|\<dot\>><rsub|t>,
        </equation*>

        then <math|Ent<rsub|\<nu\><rsub|T>><around|(|\<rho\>|)>\<leqslant\><frac|2|\<varrho\>>*\<bbb-E\><rsub|\<nu\><rsub|T>><around|\<\|\|\>|<wide|Q|\<dot\>><rsub|T><rsup|1/2>*\<mathD\><sqrt|\<rho\>>|\<\|\|\>><rsup|2>>,
        <math|<frac|1|\<varrho\>>=<big|int><rsub|0><rsup|T>\<mathe\><rsup|-2*<big|int><rsub|t><rsup|T>\<kappa\><rsub|r>*\<mathd\>r>*\<mathd\>t>.
      </theorem*>

      <\itemize>
        <item>Gradient bound at each scale + entropy formula. Gaussian check:
        <math|V<rsub|T>=0>, <math|Q<rsub|t>=t*Q<rsub|T>/T>,
        <math|\<kappa\>=0> <math|\<Rightarrow\>> Gaussian LSI.

        <item>Convexity of the <strong|effective> potentials, not of
        <math|V<rsub|T>>.

        <item>By <math|\<mathD\><rsup|2>*V<rsub|t>=S<rsub|t><rsup|-1>-S<rsub|t><rsup|-1>*Cov<rsub|t>*S<rsub|t><rsup|-1>>,
        for <math|<wide|Q|\<dot\>><rsub|t>> invertible the hypothesis is
        equivalent to the bound, uniform in <math|\<phi\>>,

        <\equation*>
          Cov<rsub|t>\<leqslant\>S<rsub|t>-S<rsub|t>*<wide|Q|\<dot\>><rsub|t><rsup|-1>*<around*|(|\<kappa\><rsub|t>*<wide|Q|\<dot\>><rsub|t>-<frac|1|2>*<wide|Q|\<ddot\>><rsub|t>|)>*<wide|Q|\<dot\>><rsub|t><rsup|-1>*S<rsub|t>:
        </equation*>

        at most <math|S<rsub|t>> iff <math|\<kappa\><rsub|t>*<wide|Q|\<dot\>><rsub|t>\<geqslant\><frac|1|2>*<wide|Q|\<ddot\>><rsub|t>>
        (linear profile: <math|\<kappa\><rsub|t>\<geqslant\>0>).
      </itemize>
    </with>
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|Poincaré from the localisation>

    <\proposition*>
      If <math|<wide|\<cal-R\>|\<dot\>><rsub|r>*Cov<rsub|\<mu\><rsub|r><rsup|\<phi\>>>*<wide|\<cal-R\>|\<dot\>><rsub|r>\<leqslant\>\<alpha\><rsub|r>*<wide|\<cal-R\>|\<dot\>><rsub|r>>
      for all <math|\<phi\>>, <math|r\<leqslant\>t>, then

      <\equation*>
        Var<rsub|\<nu\><rsub|T>><around|(|f|)>\<leqslant\>\<mathe\><rsup|<big|int><rsub|0><rsup|t>\<alpha\>>*\<bbb-E\>*Var<rsub|\<mu\><rsub|t>><around|(|f|)>,
      </equation*>

      and, for <math|\<nu\><rsub|T>> log-concave,
      <math|Var<rsub|\<nu\><rsub|T>><around|(|f|)>\<leqslant\>\<mathe\><rsup|<big|int><rsub|0><rsup|t>\<alpha\>>*\<bbb-E\><around|\<langle\>|\<mathD\>f,\<cal-R\><rsub|t><rsup|-1>*\<mathD\>f|\<rangle\>>>.
    </proposition*>

    <strong|Proof.> <math|v<around|(|r|)>=\<bbb-E\>*Var<rsub|\<mu\><rsub|r>><around|(|f|)>>
    has <math|v<rprime|'>=-\<bbb-E\><around|\<langle\>|\<chi\>,<wide|\<cal-R\>|\<dot\>>*\<chi\>|\<rangle\>>>,
    <math|\<chi\>=Cov<around|(|f,y|)>>; Cauchy\USchwarz gives
    <math|<around|\<langle\>|\<chi\>,<wide|\<cal-R\>|\<dot\>>*\<chi\>|\<rangle\>>\<leqslant\>\<alpha\>*Var<around|(|f|)>>.
    Then Brascamp\ULieb for <math|\<mu\><rsub|t>>.

    <\itemize>
      <item>Gaussian, one mode: <math|\<mathe\><rsup|<big|int>\<alpha\>>=Q<rsub|T>/S<rsub|t>>;
      equality for linear <math|f>.

      <item><strong|KLS conjecture>: isotropic log-concave on
      <math|\<bbb-R\><rsup|n>>, <math|\<cal-R\><rsub|t>=t>:
      <math|Var<around|(|f|)>\<leqslant\>t<rsup|-1>*\<mathe\><rsup|<big|int>\<alpha\>>*\<bbb-E\><around|\||\<mathD\>f|\|><rsup|2>>.
      Keep <math|<around|\<\|\|\>|Cov<rsub|r>|\<\|\|\>>> bounded as long as
      possible (only with high probability). Eldan 2013, Chen 2021,
      Klartag\ULehec 2022, Klartag 2023: Poincaré constant
      <math|O<around|(|log n|)>>.
    </itemize>
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|Two views of one martingale>

    <\with|font-size|0.9>
      <\padded-center>
        <with|font-size|0.9|<data-table|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|these
        notes>|<cell|Bauerschmidt\UBodineau>|<cell|localisation>>|<row|<cell|<math|\<nu\><rsub|t>>>|<cell|renormalised
        measure>|<cell|law of the tilt>>|<row|<cell|<math|\<mu\><rsub|t><rsup|\<phi\>>>>|<cell|fluctuation
        measure>|<cell|tilted measure>>|<row|<cell|<math|G<rsub|t>>>|<cell|Polchinski
        semigroup>|<cell|martingale <math|<big|int>\<rho\>*\<mathd\>\<mu\><rsub|t>>>>|<row|<cell|<math|\<mathD\><rsup|2>*V<rsub|t>>>|<cell|Hessian
        of the potential>|<cell|<math|S<rsub|t><rsup|-1>-S<rsub|t><rsup|-1>Cov<rsub|t>S<rsub|t><rsup|-1>>: covariance of the tilted measure>>>>>>
      </padded-center>

      <\itemize>
        <item><strong|Bridge:> <math|\<mathD\><rsup|2>*V<rsub|t>=S<rsub|t><rsup|-1>-S<rsub|t><rsup|-1>*Cov<rsub|t>*S<rsub|t><rsup|-1>>:
        convex potentials <math|=> bounded conditional covariance.

        <item><strong|Bauerschmidt\UBodineau:> Bakry\UÉmery for the
        Kolmogorov equation, curvature <math|<wide|Q|\<dot\>>*\<mathD\><rsup|2>*V<rsub|t>*<wide|Q|\<dot\>>+<frac|1|2>*<wide|Q|\<ddot\>>>:
        gradient bound at each scale, LSI at the terminal scale, far from
        log-concavity. Uniform in <math|\<phi\>>: suits the RG (sine-Gordon,
        <math|\<beta\>\<less\>6*\<pi\>>).

        <item><strong|Localisation:> bound what is lost on
        <math|<around|[|0,t|]>>, then use a known inequality for
        <math|\<mu\><rsub|t>>. Moments of the conditional law, possibly only
        with high probability (KLS).
      </itemize>

      <small|<with|color|dark grey|Bauerschmidt\UBodineau, CPAM 2021;
      Bauerschmidt\UBodineau\UDagallier, Probab. Surveys 2024; Eldan, GAFA
      2013; Chen\UEldan, FOCS 2022.>>
    </with>
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|Summary>

    \;

    <\itemize>
      <item>The <strong|Euclidean field equation>
      <math|A*\<varphi\>+V<rprime|'><around|(|\<varphi\>|)>=\<omega\>>:
      Nelson's Euclidean noise is the transpose of the derivative, fixed by
      the law of the field, not Gaussian.

      <item><strong|Field equation> at every resolution: its noise is a
      conditional expectation both of Nelson's noise and of a Gaussian bridge
      noise, hence sub-Gaussian whatever the interaction; for the forecast
      the force enters without smoothing.

      <item><strong|DS, pathwise>: an identity between stochastic
      observables, with no terminal representative needed.
    </itemize>

    \;

    <\myframed>
      <strong|Next>

      Lectures<nbsp>6\U7: a construction of <math|\<Phi\><rsup|4><rsub|3>> on
      the torus via the FBSDE.
    </myframed>
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
